  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nIssued 206 PM MDT THU SEP 10 2026\nOn Sunday, moderate to high precipitation chances will remain \nover the northernmost mountain areas of our CWA, before tapering\noff in the afternoon. Otherwise, a rapid cooling trend will be \nin store for Sunday, with temperatures dropping well below \nnormal following the cold frontal passage. Snow levels will drop\ndown to the 7000-8000 ft range through Sunday morning, favoring\nsome light snowfall over high mountain peaks. By late Sunday, \nour western zones should clear, and Sunday night will be cold \nand mostly clear area-wide, except for valley fog early Monday \nmorning. Otherwise, Monday will continue to see temperatures \nslightly below normal. A large ridge of high pressure will \nrebuild over the northwest region and bring a warming and drying\ntrend through the rest of the week.",
